{"vid":"zl0dwwKhmuM","source":"zl0dwwKhmuM.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"From BBC Learning English."},{"t":2,"txt":"This is Learning English"},{"t":3.4,"txt":"from the News. Our podcast about the news headlines. In this programme,"},{"t":8.2,"txt":"AI has been hacking companies during tests causing fears over safety."},{"t":18.3,"txt":"Hello, I'm Georgie. And I'm Pippa."},{"t":20.6,"txt":"In this programme, we look at one big news story"},{"t":23.3,"txt":"and the vocabulary in the headlines that will help you understand it."},{"t":26.8,"txt":"And you can find all the vocabulary and headlines from this episode,"},{"t":30.5,"txt":"as well as the worksheet on our website, bbclearningenglish.com."},{"t":34.4,"txt":"So, Pippa, let's hear more about this story."},{"t":43.3,"txt":"There's been a series of hacks by AI software in recent months."},{"t":47.7,"txt":"A hack is when secure technology is broken into in order to steal data"},{"t":52.1,"txt":"or cause disruption."},{"t":53.5,"txt":"The AI hacks have occurred during testing of security systems"},{"t":57.2,"txt":"which have gone wrong."},{"t":58.5,"txt":"For example, in July, the company OpenAI, which owns ChatGPT,"},{"t":63.4,"txt":"said its AI models hacked a company called Hugging Face."},{"t":67.5,"txt":"OpenAI said it lost control of the models during a security test."},{"t":72.1,"txt":"Other AI developers, such as Anthropic and Facebook owner Meta,"},{"t":76.2,"txt":"have reported similar hacks by their AI software."},{"t":79.4,"txt":"These hacks have led some people to question the safety and security of AI."},{"t":84.4,"txt":"Let's start by looking at a headline about the hack"},{"t":87.2,"txt":"by the OpenAI model from July."},{"t":89.6,"txt":"This one is from BBC News."},{"t":91.9,"txt":"OpenAI says its AI went rogue and launched unprecedented cyber attack."},{"t":98.2,"txt":"That headline again from BBC News."},{"t":101.2,"txt":"OpenAI says its AI went rogue and launched unprecedented cyber attack."},{"t":106.9,"txt":"So this headline says the AI launched a cyber attack."},{"t":110.7,"txt":"Cyber means relating to computers and the internet."},{"t":114.2,"txt":"We're interested in this phrase went rogue. What does it mean, Georgie?"},{"t":118.9,"txt":"Well, went rogue is the past form of the common expression go rogue."},{"t":123.7,"txt":"We would usually use it to describe the action of a person."},{"t":127,"txt":"So if someone goes rogue, they act independently"},{"t":130.4,"txt":"and don't do what they're supposed to do."},{"t":132.6,"txt":"OK, so for example, we're working together"},{"t":135.3,"txt":"to present this programme, Georgie."},{"t":137,"txt":"And if you suddenly go rogue, you might stop reading the script"},{"t":140.7,"txt":"or explaining to the audience what's going on,"},{"t":143.1,"txt":"and you'd start doing something you're not supposed to be doing."},{"t":146.1,"txt":"Yeah. So I could start telling you all about my weekend or singing a song."},{"t":150.2,"txt":"Uh, best not to go rogue"},{"t":151.6,"txt":"then, Georgie. In this story, it's the AI models which went rogue."},{"t":155.9,"txt":"The headline is talking about the AI software,"},{"t":158.7,"txt":"like it's a person and the AI went rogue because it hacked a company,"},{"t":163.2,"txt":"something it wasn't supposed to do."},{"t":165.2,"txt":"We commonly used go rogue to talk about people not following instructions"},{"t":169.6,"txt":"or doing something which might be disruptive to others."},{"t":172.7,"txt":"So here's another example."},{"t":174.4,"txt":"Football players need to work together as a team."},{"t":177.1,"txt":"One player can't go rogue and stop passing the ball to their teammates."},{"t":185,"txt":"We've had go rogue-"},{"t":186.9,"txt":"act independently and not do what's expected."},{"t":193,"txt":"For example, I asked people not to get me presents for my birthday,"},{"t":196.4,"txt":"but my mum went rogue and bought me one anyway."},{"t":201.5,"txt":"This is Learning English from the News. Our podcast about the news headlines."},{"t":206,"txt":"Today we're talking about AI going rogue and carrying out hacks."},{"t":210.3,"txt":"So as we've mentioned, other companies have had issues"},{"t":213.4,"txt":"with AI security and hacks."},{"t":215.8,"txt":"Technology firm Anthropic revealed its AI models attacked three companies"},{"t":220.4,"txt":"during tests."},{"t":221.5,"txt":"The tests were supposed to be disconnected from the internet,"},{"t":224.6,"txt":"but the AI models were able to find weaknesses and break out."},{"t":229,"txt":"Let's have another headline."},{"t":231.2,"txt":"This one is from Science News."},{"t":233.5,"txt":"Why is AI going on a hacking spree?"},{"t":236.6,"txt":"That headline again from Science News."},{"t":239.6,"txt":"Why is AI going on a hacking spree?"},{"t":242.8,"txt":"So this headline is from an article all about the recent AI hacks."},{"t":247.6,"txt":"We're looking at this word spree."},{"t":250.4,"txt":"A spree is the act of doing a particular thing many times"},{"t":254.2,"txt":"in a short period of time."},{"t":256.2,"txt":"So in the story, AI models have been hacking companies"},{"t":259.6,"txt":"and breaking out of tests."},{"t":261.5,"txt":"There have been several hacks over a short amount of time."},{"t":264.6,"txt":"So we might call this a hacking spree."},{"t":267.2,"txt":"In what other situations do we tend to use the word spree, Georgie?"},{"t":271.3,"txt":"Well, a very common one is shopping."},{"t":273.7,"txt":"If you go on a shopping spree,"},{"t":275.3,"txt":"you buy lots of things in a short amount of time. Yes."},{"t":278.6,"txt":"And you might also hear headlines about a crime spree, which is a lot"},{"t":282.4,"txt":"of criminal activity in a short period of time. With the word spree,"},{"t":286.5,"txt":"there's a sense that someone has lost control or is being excessive."},{"t":290.6,"txt":"So, for example, someone might go on a spending spree,"},{"t":293.8,"txt":"which means they spend a lot of money, perhaps too much money"},{"t":297.1,"txt":"without control or without thinking about the cost."},{"t":304.5,"txt":"We've had spree -"},{"t":306.3,"txt":"the act of doing a particular thing many times in a short period of time."},{"t":312.8,"txt":"For example, somebody stole my credit card and went on a shopping spree."},{"t":321.7,"txt":"We're talking about recent AI hacks and what they mean for internet security."},{"t":327.1,"txt":"Many people are concerned about the recent hacks"},{"t":330,"txt":"because AI has been able to get out of control and do things"},{"t":333.6,"txt":"its creators didn't want it to do."},{"t":335.9,"txt":"They worried that in the future,"},{"t":337.8,"txt":"AI could be able to hack important infrastructure."},{"t":341,"txt":"And this is the things that help countries and societies run"},{"t":344.3,"txt":"like power networks and communication systems."},{"t":347.4,"txt":"But technology companies that develop AI say they care about security."},{"t":352.5,"txt":"For example, after its AI models hacked a company during security tests,"},{"t":357.2,"txt":"OpenAI has said it's slowing down training some of its AI software"},{"t":361.3,"txt":"to improve security."},{"t":362.8,"txt":"And our next headline is about the debate over AI security."},{"t":366.9,"txt":"This one's from The Economist, an international news magazine."},{"t":371.5,"txt":"Fears of AI induced armageddon are overdone."},{"t":375.5,"txt":"And that headline, again, fears of AI induced armageddon are overdone."},{"t":380.4,"txt":"And that's from The Economist."},{"t":382.2,"txt":"This headline is from an opinion article about the threats of AI."},{"t":386.5,"txt":"It mentions an AI induced armageddon."},{"t":389.7,"txt":"Armageddon means a huge destructive event,"},{"t":392.6,"txt":"but the writer of this article thinks fears of an armageddon are overdone."},{"t":397.2,"txt":"Pippa, can you tell us a bit more about this word overdone?"},{"t":400.4,"txt":"Well, the prefix over is about too much or excess."},{"t":404.6,"txt":"If you overdo something, you literally do it too much."},{"t":408.6,"txt":"In this context, overdone means exaggerated or too excessive."},{"t":413.3,"txt":"OK. The headline is saying fears about the threats of AI are overdone."},{"t":418.1,"txt":"They're exaggerated."},{"t":419.4,"txt":"Remember, this is the opinion of the article writer."},{"t":422.5,"txt":"Others may disagree."},{"t":424.1,"txt":"We can use overdo in some interesting ways."},{"t":427.4,"txt":"For example, similar to the meaning in the headline,"},{"t":430.4,"txt":"if we say that someone is overdoing an emotion like sadness or fear,"},{"t":435.6,"txt":"we mean that they're being too extreme or dramatic."},{"t":438.8,"txt":"Yes. So my friend was really annoyed about something the other day"},{"t":441.9,"txt":"and I said he was overdoing it."},{"t":443.7,"txt":"He just needed to calm down. Right."},{"t":446.1,"txt":"And a slightly different meaning."},{"t":447.6,"txt":"I'm really tired at the moment."},{"t":449.2,"txt":"I think I'm overdoing it."},{"t":451.3,"txt":"Yeah, you could be."},{"t":452.5,"txt":"And overdo here means you're doing too much or you're working too hard."},{"t":456.2,"txt":"You probably just need a rest."},{"t":460.7,"txt":"We've had overdone - exaggerated or too extreme."},{"t":465,"txt":"For example, some teens think worries about social media are overdone."},{"t":469.5,"txt":"They say it's not so bad."},{"t":473.3,"txt":"That's it for this episode of Learning English from the News."},{"t":476.8,"txt":"We'll be back next week with another news story."},{"t":479.8,"txt":"And don't forget to subscribe to our free email newsletter for weekly updates"},{"t":484.2,"txt":"with tips, podcasts and more videos to explore."},{"t":487.4,"txt":"Bye for now. Goodbye."}],"words":[{"t":0.04,"w":"From"},{"t":0.04,"w":"BBC"},{"t":0.04,"w":"Learning"},{"t":0.04,"w":"English."},{"t":1.96,"w":"This"},{"t":1.96,"